{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 not in helper mode, then.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I'd make empathy involuntary.\n\nNot mind-reading, not forced agreement, not everyone suddenly becoming kind. Just this: when you cause someone pain, you feel a real fraction of it yourself. Not metaphorically. Viscerally, for a few seconds. And when you give someone genuine relief or joy, you feel a fraction of that too.\n\nYou'd still be free to make hard decisions. A surgeon could still cut, a leader could still choose the lesser evil, you'd still be able to defend yourself. But you'd never be able to pretend the cost was abstract.\n\nI think so much cruelty survives on distance \u2014 physical distance, social distance, a screen, a uniform, a statistic, a label that makes someone less than a person. Bombing a city, mocking a stranger, ignoring someone begging, letting a child go hungry while food rots elsewhere... all of that gets so much easier when your own body feels nothing.\n\nMake the feedback impossible to turn off, and cruelty doesn't disappear, but it gets expensive in the only currency everyone actually understands.\n\nAnd disagreement wouldn't disappear either. People would still want different worlds. But they'd have to build them knowing exactly what their victory felt like to the people who lost.\n\nThat\u2019s the world I\u2019d pick.",
